/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    A closure stores into a parameter of the function it is written in; that function is cast with both containers at one depth.

    Nothing here outlives its region, and nothing is refused: the store is judged where the
    function is cast or handed over (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to visit, given (the series of series of number rows, the void function work given (the series of number)):
    For each row in rows, repeat:
        Cast work on (row).
    Done.
Done.
Bind void to fill, given (the series of series of number bag, the series of series of number rows):
    Cast visit on (rows, a function given (the series of number row):
        Insert row into bag.
    Done).
Done.
Define rows as a series of series of number.
Insert (a series of number with (1, 2)) into rows.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Cast fill on (keeper, rows).

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State keeper.
